From 05b9741665d08d401a58cefc81ce4c1087f2aa3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:51:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] cards: put the task first and name the tests the
 repository keeps

The showcase's http-header family passed 14/16 in control and 4/16 with Adage:
its four training sessions wrote no test, so the learned card listed only
name.rs and mod.rs, and agents treated it as the whole job, skipping the test
their task asked for.

- The card's first line now says what it is (what earlier sessions did, not
  the complete procedure) and that the task's own requirements come first:
  do everything it asks (for example tests), even where earlier sessions did not.
- A card names the test files the repository keeps for its source files
  (testmap::tests_of: name, co-change, traces; then testmap::nearby: tests
  named for the file or its directory, for checkouts without history), at
  most 3, leaving out the card's own files.
- A card is marked `untested` when no trace of the family changed a test file
  while the repository keeps tests for its files; the tests line says so.
- Regression tests: an http-like family whose sessions never touch tests
  (and one whose sessions do; and one without a checkout), rendering, budget,
  checks, and old indexes reading as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
