+  "http-header--timing-allow-origin": "Add a constant for the `Timing-Allow-Origin` header to the http crate: `http::header::TIMING_ALLOW_ORIGIN`. It lists the origins allowed to see timing values retrieved via the Resource Timing API.\n\nIt must be a standard header name like the crate's other header constants: parsing the name in any letter case gives the constant, for example `HeaderName::from_bytes(b\"Timing-Allow-Origin\")` equals `header::TIMING_ALLOW_ORIGIN`, and `header::TIMING_ALLOW_ORIGIN.as_str()` is `\"timing-allow-origin\"`.\n\nInclude tests, and document the constant, as the project does for its other standard headers.",
+  "http-header--repr-digest": "Add a constant for the `Repr-Digest` header to the http crate: `http::header::REPR_DIGEST`. It carries a digest of the selected representation of the target resource.\n\nIt must be a standard header name like the crate's other header constants: parsing the name in any letter case gives the constant, for example `HeaderName::from_bytes(b\"Repr-Digest\")` equals `header::REPR_DIGEST`, and `header::REPR_DIGEST.as_str()` is `\"repr-digest\"`.\n\nInclude tests, and document the constant, as the project does for its other standard headers.",
+  "http-header--early-data": "Add a constant for the `Early-Data` header to the http crate: `http::header::EARLY_DATA`. It indicates that the request was conveyed in TLS early data (0-RTT).\n\nIt must be a standard header name like the crate's other header constants: parsing the name in any letter case gives the constant, for example `HeaderName::from_bytes(b\"Early-Data\")` equals `header::EARLY_DATA`, and `header::EARLY_DATA.as_str()` is `\"early-data\"`.\n\nInclude tests, and document the constant, as the project does for its other standard headers."
+ },
